;
MAKING THE SYSTEM YOUR OWN

A - The sign-on message
B - Maintaining HELP
:A
THE SIGN-ON MESSAGE

BYE displays A0:WELCOME.TXT when a caller calls.
From private CP/M, enter:

    SYSUTLS:ZDE A0:WELCOME.TXT

ZDE uses WordStar editing keys.
Ctrl-K S saves; Ctrl-K X saves and exits; Ctrl-K Q abandons edits.
Keep the caller blanked until editing and saving are finished.
The revised welcome appears on the next call.
Keep it short enough that a regular caller won't dread reading it.
:B
MAINTAINING HELP

HELP topics live in I14:HELP and use the HELPC plain-text format.
HELP opens HELP.HLP; HELP topic opens the named topic directly.

A semicolon on the first line starts the file. An index may link
to another file with :A:AUTH.HLP or introduce a section with :A.
Keep indexes within one screen and all lines within 78 columns.
Information sections are paginated automatically.

Use ASCII text with CRLF line endings and Ctrl-Z EOF. Maintain
the source files as well as the installed copies. No passwords
or private installation details belong in public HELP.
